#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2005 |author=Sean Dooley|title=The Big Twitch|page=182|text=Dave comes across like an '''ocker''' Australian.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|2007|Phillip William Hughes|Opening Doors to the Future: Stories of Prominent Australians and the Influence of Teachers|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=W9DDUKherEgC&pg=PA133&dq=%22more|most+ocker%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=6X3DT97lN4-6iAfLqI20Cg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22more|most%20ocker%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=133|text=In addition to these specialist skills he showed his individuality at school where he preferred karate to rugby and when his more '''ocker''' classmates went to celebrate in pubs he went with a friend to Chinese restaurants.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|2008|Robert Crawford|But Wait, There's More!: A History of Australian Advertising, 1900-2000|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=281H7JjhOo4C&pg=PA179&dq=%22more|most+ocker%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=6X3DT97lN4-6iAfLqI20Cg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22more|most%20ocker%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=179|text=Singo′s subsequent campaigns became more creative, developing a louder, brasher, and decidedly more '''ocker''' image in the process.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|2008|David P. Reiter|Primary Instinct|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=1jp4D3NwsHgC&pg=PA93&dq=%22more|most+ocker%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=6X3DT97lN4-6iAfLqI20Cg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22more|most%20ocker%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=93|text=His name is Bob Snapes, and you don′t get any more '''ocker''' than him.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|2011 January 25|Emily Portell||[[w:Herald Sun|Herald Sun]]|location=Melbourne|text=Melbourne surf shop Mordy Surf triggered outrage after posting the YouTube clip, in which an '''ocker''' man says he is "gonna get a glass and smash it on some poof", on its website.}}

